# Ignore file for Dockerfile.nerdbot builds ONLY (BuildKit picks
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore over .dockerignore for `-f Dockerfile.nerdbot`).
# The stock .dockerignore excludes user_data/, which this image exists to
# ship - so this file whitelists exactly the Nerdbot overlay directories.
# The stock Dockerfile and .dockerignore are deliberately untouched.
#
# SECURITY: docker does NOT honor .gitignore, so a developer checkout may
# contain untracked files with credentials (user_data/config.json, local
# sqlite/log/data files). Only the four tracked overlay directories are
# sent to the build context - nothing else under user_data/ can ever be
# baked into an image layer.

# Exclude everything ...
*

# ... except the tracked Nerdbot overlay directories.
!user_data/exchange/
!user_data/scripts/
!user_data/strategies/
!user_data/config_templates/

# Belt-and-braces recursive re-includes: moby/patternmatcher applies
# parent-directory matching to negated patterns, so the directory forms
# above should already re-include the files beneath them - but a build
# cannot be exercised in this environment (registry egress blocked), so
# the explicit ** forms remove any dependence on that behavior.
!user_data/exchange/**
!user_data/scripts/**
!user_data/strategies/**
!user_data/config_templates/**

# CI-generated sample strategies and build-context junk must never ship.
# These stay LAST so they win over the re-includes above.
user_data/strategies/Awesome*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.sqlite
**/*.log
